{
  "note": "Release 1.16.2 facts answerer (brain/facts.ts): which kind of question about the user's own saved numbers a message is. Matched like phrases.json (whole words on normalized text, a trailing 's' always allowed, '*' = any word ending). A message is a fact question only when it has a '?' or doesn't start with a 'statementStarts' word ('I had a big lunch' is a statement; 'tip for the dumbbell row' and 'calories remaining' are questions), doesn't start with an 'adviceStarts' phrase, has no 'block', 'advice' or 'otherPeople' phrase, and a kind's every 'all' group has a hit and none of its 'none' phrases. Kinds are tried in order; the first hit wins. 'exercise': 'required' = the message must name an exercise, 'none' = it must not, 'any' = either. 'day': 'required' = it must name a day (today, tomorrow, a weekday). Unknown → no kind → the model answers as before. Advice and judgement questions ('Should I train hard today?', 'what should I do', 'is my form ok', 'too heavy') and 'plan my…' requests go to the model, which has the plan line and the Lighter-today reasons; a question about someone else's numbers ('my wife', 'she') never gets the user's. 'What weight should I use on X' is a lookup (planned), not advice. Someone else's numbers are also caught structurally: an 'auxiliaries' word followed by a subject that isn't I / you / my / me (facts.ts) and isn't a 'notSubjects' word, a day, a number or an exercise ('What did she lift…', 'how much has he eaten') → null.",
